---
// src/pages/human-ai-interaction.astro
import SectionedPageLayout from '../layouts/SectionedPageLayout.astro';
---

<SectionedPageLayout title="Human-AI Interaction">
  <section
    id="problem"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex md:items-stretch gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="problem-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="problem-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Problem</h2>
      <p>
        Live captioning is very cognitively demanding task, such that self-reported measures found captioning to be more stressful than
        surgery. 
      </p>
      <p>To mitigate these demands and improve not just working conditions of live captioners in broadcast environments but also 
        viewing outcomes of Deaf and Hard-of-Hearing audiences, a paradigm shift was proposed. 
      </p>
      <p>
        Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR) has already replaced captioners in online meetings and post-production events. As such, it follows
        that AI/ASR based captioning using modern LLMs can improve live captioning when performed with a human captioner.
      </p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%] md:flex md:flex-col mt-6 md:mt-0">
      <figure class="flex-1 flex flex-col min-h-0">
        <video
          src="/videos/live_cc_issues.mp4"
          controls
          class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto md:flex-1 md:min-h-0 md:h-full object-contain"
          aria-label="Problem diagram video"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
        <figcaption class="mt-2 shrink-0 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Live captioning is intense-- can you spot the multiple mistakes made by professional captioners?
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="methods"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex md:items-stretch gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="methods-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="methods-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Methods</h2>
      <p>
        Modern LLMs are trained on massive datasets and act as probablistic engines-- they are biased towards the majority and choose 
        the most statistically likely token to output. Marginalized populations, such as Deaf and Hard-of-Hearing audiences, make up 
        a much smaller share of the data and their needs and voices are diminished by this probablistic reasoning so a Human-in-the-Loop 
        is required-- not just for evaluation and checking, but as experts of their craft who use AI as a tool. As a reminder, LLMs rely 
        on text, sound and images-- they cannot replicate human learning as a multi--sensory experience (I have written about this elsewhere).
      </p>
      <p>
        Executed a study drawing from psychology, cognitive science, computer science and industrial engineering to conduct a
        study where captioners supervised AI to write captions rather than working alone
      </p>
      <p>
        Mixed-methods approach with 21 captioners using NASA-TLX, System Usability Scale, Nielsen-Norman Satisfaction
        Scale, Trust in Automation Scale and qualitative interviews
      </p>
      <p>Time-series-- 3 sessions spaced 24 hours apart to allow for learning</p>
      <p>Controlled environment and pre-screened for familiarity</p>
      <p>Two independent groups: Novices and Experts-- controlled for skill level</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%] md:flex md:flex-col mt-6 md:mt-0">
      <figure class="flex-1 flex flex-col min-h-0">
        <img
          src="/images/methods.png"
          alt="Research Methods"
          class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto md:flex-1 md:min-h-0 md:h-full object-contain"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 shrink-0 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Used a cross-disciplinary approach to develop measurements for 14 constructs in the Human Autonomy System
          Oversight model (which until now was theoretical).
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="findings"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex md:items-stretch gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="findings-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="findings-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Findings</h2>
      <p>Mitigating fear is about expectation management</p>
      <p>Captioners desire more control over AI</p>
      <p>AI reduced physical and mental workload over just 3 sessions spaced 24 hours apart</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%] md:flex md:flex-col mt-6 md:mt-0">
      <figure class="flex-1 flex flex-col min-h-0">
        <img
          src="/images/findings.png"
          alt="Findings"
          class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto md:flex-1 md:min-h-0 md:h-full object-contain"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 shrink-0 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Saw a statistically significant reduction in mental workload, which led me to test and discover relationships
          not present in the original model.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="recommendations"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex md:items-stretch gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="recommendations-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="recommendations-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Recommendations</h2>
      <p>Human benefit from control over AI</p>
      <p>Even if AI can automate the job, manual control should be relegated</p>
      <p>Scheduling is one recommended solution</p>
      <p>Another is interface based (see Design Mock-up from the side menu)</p>
      <p> Why involve a human captioner at all? Research shows that human+AI working conditions produce the best results, 
        and captioning is more than just transcription.
      </p>
      <p>
        Captioning is the art of understanding what information needs to be conveyed to the audience and requires cultural understanding, human judgement and 
        first-hand experience serving Deaf and Hard-of-Hearing audiences. 
      </p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%] md:flex md:flex-col mt-6 md:mt-0">
      <figure class="flex-1 flex flex-col min-h-0">
        <img
          src="/images/loa.png"
          alt="Recommendations"
          class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto md:flex-1 md:min-h-0 md:h-full object-contain"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 shrink-0 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Based on rigorous analysis, I suggested a model where control and automation is adaptive to user needs. This
          has far-reaching implications for human use over AI.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="impact"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex md:items-stretch gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="impact-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="impact-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Impact</h2>
      <p>Led the only study on captioners supervising AI in the world</p>
      <p>Broadcasting agencies and governments are not prepared for this inevitable shift so I took matters into my own hands. I established 
        Captioners as Supervisors of AI, promoting them from a role of operator to a role of delegator and judge. By combining human and AI talent,
        we get the best of both worlds: the tireless efficiency of AI and the priceless judgement and experience of humans.
      </p>
      <p>Discovered new relationships between Human-AI constructs and made novel contributions</p>
      <p>Developed a reproducible and transferrable model for all AI assisted workflows to guide superior Human-AI Interfaces 
        and maximize the potential of Human-AI collaboration. The future is Human-AI and I can help you implement evidence-based 
        solutions.
      </p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%] md:flex md:flex-col mt-6 md:mt-0">
      <figure class="flex-1 flex flex-col min-h-0">
        <img
          src="/images/impact.png"
          alt="Impact"
          class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto md:flex-1 md:min-h-0 md:h-full object-contain"
        />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 shrink-0 text-sm text-gray-600">
          I discovered three new relationships which better explain Human-AI Interaction contrary to theory.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="publication"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex md:items-stretch gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="publication-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="publication-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Presentation</h2>
      <p>
        The culmination of my work was presented to key stakeholders, including the CEOs of 3PlayMedia and ScribeWire,
        representatives from broadcasters and providers (i.e Rogers) and advocacy groups
      </p>
      <p>Successfully defended at Toronto Metropolitan University</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%] md:flex md:flex-col mt-6 md:mt-0">
      <figure class="flex-1 flex flex-col min-h-0">
        <iframe
          src="/docs/ai-captioning-presentation.pdf"
          class="w-full h-[360px] md:flex-1 md:min-h-0 md:h-full rounded-xl border"
          title="Thesis Defense"
        ></iframe>
        <figcaption class="mt-2 shrink-0 text-sm text-gray-600">Thesis presentation delivered to my defense committee.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</SectionedPageLayout>